  "answer": "The Dean mentions John Cox, the author of 'The Horse and its Ailments', in relation to veterinary remedies in the play. He refers to the book when he decides to administer a Bolus to the horse, and later he tells Sir Tristram to remember the little volume and its humane author, John Cox.",
